The table of power-off codes (src/model/tvbgone_codes.cpp) is not covered by the
MIT license above. It is converted from WORLDcodes.c of the TV-B-Gone kit
firmware v1.2, (c) Mitch Altman + Limor Fried 2009
(https://github.com/adafruit/TV-B-Gone-kit), and is distributed, like the
original, under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported
license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

The conversion (Tools/generar_codigos.py) unpacks the bit-packed indices and
stores the carrier frequencies in hertz; the codes themselves are unchanged.

TV-B-Gone is a trademark of Cornfield Electronics. This project is an
independent port and is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.
